          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On Saturday, August 29, 2015 at 21:26, a witness on their terrace was observing the stars and an airplane, and was surprised to see in the northwest a luminous phenomenon increase and then decrease in intensity until disappearing. Only one testimony was collected. The witness reported the following characteristics of PAN: - A stationary bright point \n- Observation duration of 10 seconds\n- Brightness similar to that of a star\n\nThese data are typical of a flare or flash Iridium. Furthermore, the data regarding the time and direction of the observation (exact time noted as 21:26 and observation direction towards the northwest) align with those concerning the Iridium flare of the Iridium 54 object, which had a maximum magnitude of -6.6 (see the investigation note). \n\nTherefore, GEIPAN classifies the case as A: observation of an Iridium flare.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "306d7e74a021eb6f3afd80b42b4e38f10fc78230d263be19358996c1b359980e"
        }
